Application will give you ARM_CLIENT_ID and ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID
when you create the certificate and secret it gives you secret_id and value (we need value here)
At subscription you get the ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID

steps:
- Goto --- Azure Portal --- Azure Entra ID --- App Registrations --- New Registration --- terraform-iac(name can be anything) this will give us ARM_CLIENT_ID and ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID

- Goto --- Azure Portal --- Subscriptions --- Access Control (IAM) --- Add Role Assignment --- previledged role --- contributor --- assign to ---  add members --- search for the app registration you created ie terraform-iac and assign

#Now create the secret value
- Goto --- IAM --- App Registrations --- terraform-iac --- Certificates & Secrets --- New Client Secret --- 90 days ---create (copy the secret value)


Once you get export these values into your environment variables, you can use them to authenticate with Azure.
